<h1>Universal Gripper Control System</h1>
<p class="lead">Development of a modular control system for a robotic gripper, integrating motor actuation, sensing and ROS 2.</p>
</section>
<section class="page-shell detail-layout">
<div class="detail-copy">
<h2>Project overview</h2>
<p>This project focuses on the development of a control architecture for a universal robotic gripper. The system combines electromechanical actuation, sensor integration and software interfaces to support controlled grasping.</p>
<h2>Engineering activities</h2>
<ul class="clean-list">
<li>Integration and control of the gripper motor.</li>
<li>Development of ROS 2 packages and interfaces for hardware communication.</li>
<li>Integration of tactile sensors to support contact detection and grasp interaction.</li>
<li>Implementation of gripper commands, feedback and safety-related limits.</li>
<li>Development of a modular architecture for testing and future extensions.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Technologies</h2>
<p>ROS 2, Python, motor control, CAN communication and tactile sensing.</p>
